From 58c55fc250d2ac245b861188fa694ffb92ca8083 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gemini Wi-Fi experiment (non-certifying)" <noreply@gemini-wifi.invalid>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 16:33:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wmt: guard one patch-search reply in the isolated experiment

Userspace can be delayed between a deadline check and its reply write.
Accept only the first patch-search transaction of this experiment boot
and serialize reply acceptance against expiry and terminal state.

Initialize the reply signal and command before exposing the pending bit.
Refuse late or duplicate replies and propagate refusal through WMT_write.
Never reset the consumed transaction within this boot. Other userspace
WMT command types are outside the isolated BTIF startup protocol.

This deliberately restricts the vendor experiment. It is not an
upstream API proposal or device candidate. No DCO is asserted.
---
 .../common_main/core/include/wmt_ctrl.h       |  1 +
 .../common/common_main/core/wmt_ctrl.c        | 88 +++++++++++++------
 .../common/common_main/core/wmt_lib.c         |  7 +-
 .../common/common_main/linux/wmt_dev.c        |  7 +-
 4 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

